# Indent each body line with one tab; use $1, ${1:default}, and $0 for placeholders.
# Backticks evaluate Vim expressions, such as `strftime("%Y-%m-%d")`.
snippet note note
	---
	date: [`strftime("%H:%M, %Y-%m-%d")`]
	---
	
	$0
	
	
	[#tag]()
	
	---
	
	## Connections

snippet daily daily
	---
	date: [`strftime("%H:%M, %Y-%m-%d")`]
	---
	
	
	# Today's Schedule
	
	- [ ] $0
	
	# Things to remember 
	
	- [ ] 

snippet writing writing template
    ## Reading list:

    - $0

    ## Outline:

    1. Topic

    ## First Draft:

    In the begining, there was foo.

    ## Sentence rewrite:

    Original sentence

    - Alternatives

    ## Favorite sentences:

    Lucky sentences.

    ## Rearranged sentences:

    Lucky sentences with their new order

    ## Combined sentences forming paragraphs:

    Paragraphs

    ## Rearragned paragraph leading to the Second Draft:

    Rearranged paragraphs.

snippet pandoc pandoc
	---
	title: "$1"
	author: "$2"
	date: \today
	geometry: margin=1in
	documentclass: extarticle
	fontsize: 12pt
	linkcolor: blue
	numbersections: false
	mainfont: "Times New Roman"
	monofont: "Courier New"
	header-includes:
	    - \usepackage{titlesec}
	    - \titleformat{\section}{\LARGE\bfseries\centering}{\thesection}{1em}{}
	    - \titleformat{\subsection}{\Large\bfseries}{\thesection}{1em}{}
	---
	
	$0
